From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Rouesnel <wrouesnel@wrouesnel.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:45:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ctl: Don't crash when the gnome-remote-desktop user doesn't
 exist

grdctl looks up the gnome-remote-desktop system user to tell whether
it's running as the system daemon's user, and dereferenced the result
without checking it.

Build environments often don't have that user, so the grdctl test
crashed there.

Treat a missing user as not running as it.

(cherry picked from commit deb332fd591cb4230c93b7477499ad8855531c6e)
---
 src/grd-ctl.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/grd-ctl.c b/src/grd-ctl.c
index 9c9b4eb..996106f 100644
--- a/src/grd-ctl.c
+++ b/src/grd-ctl.c
@@ -1182,7 +1182,7 @@ main (int   argc,
     }
 
   pw = getpwnam (GRD_USERNAME);
-  if (geteuid () == pw->pw_uid)
+  if (pw && geteuid () == pw->pw_uid)
     runtime_mode = GRD_RUNTIME_MODE_SYSTEM;
 
   settings = create_settings (runtime_mode);
